#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Aegis on rootless Podman: the host installer and its Quadlet unit renderer.

The operator runs this file with the host's system Python (3.11 or newer), outside any
checkout, so it imports only the standard library. Bootstrap copies just this script out of
the release's backend image (spec D4); ``init`` and ``upgrade`` then extract that release's
own ``/usr/share/aegis/podman/`` and render with its renderer and templates, so the units
always come from the release they install.

Rendering: the Quadlet templates live in ``quadlet/``. Their only substitution syntax is
``@@NAME@@``, every value is validated before it reaches a unit file, and an unknown or
leftover token fails the whole render. The units need systemd 254 or newer (RestartSteps=,
RestartMaxDelaySec= and RestartMode=).

Installing: the installer creates, changes and removes only what its record names, by exact
path, identity or object name, never by pattern. Every program runs through one runner as an
argument vector; there is no shell and no sudo. The privileged host steps (the SELinux module
and the firewall rules) go into a script the operator reviews and runs with sudo.
"""
